# D-93 revised — `offer_unavailable`, notice in the bar (session 6a, 2026-11-09)

Approved by Apurva (D-93, placement revised). Not in `ui-screens/` yet: the picture joins the D-94 refresh and is copied there at D-94 step 5, after the main thread's go-ahead.

**State:** the phone answers "unavailable" when the doctor taps **Turn on**. The offer screen stays as it was (title, subtitle, fingerprint tile, three points). The bar shows the warning notice `alert-triangle` / `unlock.unavailable` "Faster sign-in isn't available on this phone right now." in the same slot as Offline and "Couldn't turn on". The primary (`#turn-on`) reads **Continue** (`offer.continue`) → Home. Not now is hidden. Phone Back = Continue. Not enabled; recorded as offered.

**Changed:** `ui-screens/faster-signin-offer/faster-signin-offer.html` (top-of-panel notice and the separate Continue button removed; the `unavailable` variant uses the bar notice; the session-5 `id="hero-wrap"` removed again) · `app/screens/faster-signin-offer.js` / `.css` (same) · `ui-screens/app-logic.md` §2 (offer outcomes and the A-19 notice-placement paragraph) · `docs/feedback-state-map.md` row `offer.unavailable` · `docs/layout_check.py --app` (`offer_unavailable` checks `#turn-on`) · `tests/entry-journeys.mjs` F5d (rewritten for the bar), F5 / F5e unchanged in logic.

**Evidence (this folder; all captures use the D-94 capture settings: `capture-d93.py`, `compare-d93.mjs`):**
| Check | Result |
|---|---|
| Built app vs new picture, 390 and 360 (`compare-d93.json`, `pair_*.png`) | **0 px** at both widths |
| Six other offer states: pre-edit source (git HEAD) vs edited source (`regress-head/`, `regress/`, `regress.json`) | **12 / 12 identical** |
| New picture vs approved concept at 390 (`concept-vs-render.json`, `concept-vs-render_w390.png`) | same size · 0 shifted rows · 0 colour bands · max channel 102 · 11,396 px over 8/255 (1,915 in the bar, 9,481 above it) · **every one on a glyph or corner edge** (0 changed pixels in flat areas on either side) |

**Difference to list (brief 6a.3):** the edge-smoothing count against the concept (11,396 px) is above the session-4 limit (3,000 px). It is spread over the whole screen, including the unchanged title and points, and it is edge-only with no shift and no band. So it comes from how the concept was captured (route not recorded; not the D-94 settings), not from the design. For comparison, the approved `offer_fingerprint` vs its D-94 re-render differs by 111 px. No other difference: same layout, notice, icon, wrap ("Faster sign-in isn't available / on this phone right now."), button and colours.

Sheet: `concept-vs-render_w390.png` (concept | new picture | changed pixels).
# D-94 baseline check — old approved pictures vs new renders (session 6, 2026-11-09)

Old = `ui-screens/` (128 old-Mac pictures + 20 D-92 new-Mac). New = `session-6/new/`, rendered from the approved sources with the D-94 capture
(`capture-method-cap.py`: fixed flags `--font-render-hinting=none --disable-gpu --disable-lcd-text --force-color-profile=srgb
--disable-font-subpixel-positioning --disable-partial-raster --disable-skia-runtime-opts --hide-scrollbars`, DPR 2 from the page, fixed clock,
animations frozen, fonts loaded + two frames). Measured by `picdiff.py` (per picture: changed px, px over 8/255, max channel, shifted rows,
colour bands). **Same design** = same size, 0 shifted rows, 0 colour bands, ≤ 3,000 px over 8/255 and max ≤ 110 (session-4 limits).

## Repeatable capture (step 1)

All pictures captured twice with the D-94 settings (`session-6/new/` vs a second run): **{"identical": 296}** (`repeat-check.json`). The compare (`tests/compare-step1.mjs`) uses the same flags and captures each picture once (retry loop removed).

Two things had to change to get there:
- **Flags.** `--force-device-scale-factor=2` (an example flag in the brief) re-scales text on top of the page DPR and moved every glyph:
  ~23,000–48,000 px over 8/255 with shifted rows on every picture. It is not used. `--disable-gpu` is the flag that matters: GPU raster
  gave come-and-go noise between captures (seen in sessions 3–5), and software raster is also much closer to the old-Mac pictures
  (sign-in 1,660 → 65 px).
- **One source race (`ui-screens/case/case.html`, `a-confirm-busy`).** The secondary row (greyed Callback) was hidden or shown depending
  on when a ResizeObserver in the old `app.js` fired (about 1 capture in 4 showed it). The approved picture has it hidden; the recipe
  now hides it explicitly, as `a-confirm-failed` already did. No approved picture changes (same pixels as the approved look; 0 / 10 probes showed the row).

## Old vs new (step 3)

Pictures compared: 296 · result: **{"same design": 294, "identical": 2, "NEW (not in old)": 2}** (`baseline-check.json`).

New picture with no old one (approved D-93, joins `ui-screens/` at step 5): `faster-signin-offer/offer_unavailable_w360.png`, `faster-signin-offer/offer_unavailable_w390.png`.

**Every picture is the same design** (no shifted row, no colour band, inside the limits). None is held back.

Largest: `returning-unlock/unlock_pending_w360.png` 2062 px over 8 · highest channel difference: `case/a-confirm-busy_w360.png` 103.

